      "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\r\n\r\n# What does this PR do?\r\n  With `delay_wgrad_compute=True`, Transformer Engine marks weights with `skip_backward_post_hook`. MFSDP v2 relies on this marker to reduce them after `backward_dw()`. When MFSDP v2 materializes or shards parameters, it copies only the attributes in `_PARAMETER_ATTRIBUTES_TO_PRESERVE`, so the marker was lost for  modules built on the meta device. Gradients were then reduced before `backward_dw()` ran.\r\n\r\n This PR adds `skip_backward_post_hook` to that list.\r\n\r\n\r\n  ## Testing\r\n ` test_mcore_dense.py::test_delayed_wgrad_matches_immediate[meta]` builds a delayed-wgrad `te.Linear` on the meta device, wraps it in FullyShardedDataParallel v2, and requires bitwise-equal losses against immediate wgrad over 5 steps of 3 accumulated microbatches. It fails on main with Missing gradient for FSDP parameter ('weight',) and passes with this fix.",
      "changedFiles": 2,
